{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-220279-r4615155","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Spicy Roast Brisket","sourcePageId":220279,"sourceRevision":"4615155","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-02-03T02:26:58Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Spicy%20Roast%20Brisket&oldid=4615155","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:17:42.816Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Braised recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Main course recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using beef brisket","Category:Recipes using beef broth and stock","Category:Recipes using bell pepper","Category:Recipes using brown sugar"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"93dea5b47e51d4b8252bb55975ccdb51811f4a9648681ec3e4027063c7de44c1","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Meat recipes\n| Servings = 4–6\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Beef|Beef]]\n\nThis recipe is for a '''spicy beef brisket roast'''. It may be served with [[Cookbook:Potato|mashed potatoes]].\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|vegetable oil]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Kilogram|kg]] (2 [[Cookbook:Pound|pound]]) piece of [[Cookbook:Beef#Brisket|beef brisket]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]] or coarsely-chopped [[Cookbook:Onion|onions]]\n* 1 cup thinly sliced stalk of [[Cookbook:Celery|celery]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]] [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]] cloves\n* 1 tsp toasted, ground [[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin]] seeds\n* ½ tsp cracked [[Cookbook:Pepper|black peppercorns]]\n* 2 tsp dry [[Cookbook:Mustard|mustard]] powder\n* 2 tsp dried [[Cookbook:Oregano|oregano]] leaves\n* ½ tsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 2 cups of diced [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]], fresh or canned\n* ¼–½ cup [[Cookbook:Stock|beef stock]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Vinegar|red wine vinegar]]\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Sugar|brown sugar]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Bay leaf|bay leaves]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Bell Pepper|bell pepper]], green or red, thinly sliced\n* 1 medium or hot [[Cookbook:Chili Pepper|chile pepper]] (optional)\n== Procedure ==\n\n# Heat oil in large heavy pot, add brisket, and brown on all sides.\n# Push meat to the side. Add onions and celery, and cook over medium heat until softened.\n# Add garlic, cumin, peppercorns, mustard, oregano, salt, and stir in.\n# Add tomatoes, beef stock, vinegar, sugar, and bay leaves. Add the tomato juice if desired.\n# Add 1 cup of [[Cookbook:Boiling|boiling]] water, cover pot, and cook for 2 hours on low heat.\n# Inspect regularly to make sure there is enough liquid, adding water if necessary.\n# 30 minutes before serving, add bell and chili peppers.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* If using a larger piece of brisket, adjust other quantities accordingly.\n* While cooking, do not add cold liquid to the meat, and make sure to pour not cold tomatoes on top of the meat. Otherwise, the meat can become hard.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using beef brisket]]\n[[Category:Braised recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using whole cumin]]\n[[Category:Recipes using beef broth and stock]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mustard powder]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Spicy Roast Brisket","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"4–6","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 tbsp vegetable oil","sourceText":"1 tbsp vegetable oil","amountText":"1 tbsp vegetable oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 kg (2 pound) piece of beef brisket","sourceText":"1 kg (2 pound) piece of beef brisket","amountText":"1 kg (2 pound) piece of beef brisket","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 cup sliced or coarsely-chopped onions","sourceText":"1 cup sliced or coarsely-chopped onions","amountText":"1 cup sliced or coarsely-chopped onions","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 cup thinly sliced stalk of celery","sourceText":"1 cup thinly sliced stalk of celery","amountText":"1 cup thinly sliced stalk of celery","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"2 tsp minced garlic cloves","sourceText":"2 tsp minced garlic cloves","amountText":"2 tsp minced garlic cloves","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 tsp toasted, ground cumin seeds","sourceText":"1 tsp toasted, ground cumin seeds","amountText":"1 tsp toasted, ground cumin seeds","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"½ tsp cracked black peppercorns","sourceText":"½ tsp cracked black peppercorns","amountText":"½ tsp cracked black peppercorns","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"2 tsp dry mustard powder","sourceText":"2 tsp dry mustard powder","amountText":"2 tsp dry mustard powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"2 tsp dried oregano leaves","sourceText":"2 tsp dried oregano leaves","amountText":"2 tsp dried ore